<!--
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Atalaia contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

The default network policy (security review APP-3, decision PD11 as the
maintainer changed it: prefer HTTPS). Cleartext is refused for everything
except the few addresses where a console is served over plain HTTP:

- this phone's own console (the phone as the field controller shows it in a
  web view at the loopback address), and the emulator's host alias;
- the Pi controller's default access-point address and its mDNS name, for the
  GM console in a web view (the web view does not know the field's own CA, so
  the https console is not an option there).

Only the system's web view and Java networking read this file. The app's own
clients (check-in, player token, prop link, the site server, the feed) are
Dart's dart:io and never ask it: they pin the field CA over https in code
(field_trust.dart) and the site server's client refuses http except to the
loopback (controller_sync.dart). A field that serves its console on another
address over plain HTTP builds the app with -Patalaia.cleartextLan=true, which
picks network_security_config_lan.xml (see app/README.md, "Network policy").
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">localhost</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">127.0.0.1</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">10.0.2.2</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">192.168.4.1</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">atalaia.local</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
